Why I Use Alpine in Docker Images (And You Should Too!)

When it comes to container images, lighter is smarter 💡
That’s why I often choose alpine as my base image. Here’s why:

✅ Super Lightweight (~5MB only!)
✅ Faster builds & deployments
✅ Reduced attack surface = Better security
✅ Perfect for minimal setups & microservices

Example:
FROM alpine  
RUN apk add --no-cache python3 py3-pip

🚫 Stop pulling full Ubuntu images just to say hello.
🏋️♀️ Start pulling Alpine — light, fast, and clean.

Because in containers, every MB counts! 😎
